# Asking RMBS loan data questions in plain English: results

A language model turns each question into a small query spec, and a compiler turns the spec into SQL over governed metric definitions, so the model never does the arithmetic. These results are from a working prototype on synthetic data: {{n_deals}} Australian RMBS deals, {{n_loans}} loans and {{n_loan_months}} loan-months in 2 trustee formats.

## What is proved

| check | result |
|---|---|
| Cleaning: canonical table against simulated truth | {{canonical_truth_mismatches}} mismatches over {{n_loan_months}} loan-months |
| Cleaning: resubmitted duplicates removed | {{n_resubmission_duplicates}} of {{n_raw_rows}} raw rows |
| Cleaning: clean-up calls coded as repayments, recovered | {{n_called_deals_b}} deals |
| Compiler: output against hand-written SQL | {{gold_matched}} of {{gold_total}} match, worst difference {{gold_worst_diff}} |
| Compiler: queries that render to Oracle | {{oracle_ok}} of {{gold_total}} |
| Scale: slowest question at {{rows_36x}} loan-months | under {{x36_max_default_s}} s with default threads |

